-- title:
--   Cellwise constant germ of the local weighted discrepancy
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be an extension of number fields that is finite and Galois, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, and assume $[L:K]$ is prime. Let $v$ be a nonzero prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, let $\varphi$ be a locally constant, compactly supported function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ and $f$ a locally constant, compactly supported function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$, and assume $\varphi$ and $f$ are matching at $v$ in the sense of [`AutomorphicForm.AreMatchingLocal`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L386): twisted orbital integrals of $\varphi$ at $\delta$ agree with orbital integrals of $f$ at a regular semisimple $\gamma$ whenever $\gamma$ is the $\sigma$-norm of $\delta$ via a norm conjugator and the Haar measures on the centralizer and the $\sigma$-twisted centralizer are coupled, while orbital integrals of $f$ vanish at regular semisimple $\gamma$ that are not norms. Then there exist a function $\Psi$ on $K_v^\times\times K_v^\times$, a neighbourhood $U$ of $1$ in $K_v^\times$ and a real $\rho>0$ with the following three properties. First, $\Psi(a',t')=\Psi(a,t)$ whenever $t\in U$, $\|a'-a\|\le\rho\|a\|$ and $\|t'-t\|\le\rho\|1-t\|$. Second, there is a constant $C$ with $\|\Psi(a,t)-\Psi(a,1)\|\le C\,\|1-t\|\,(1+|\log\|1-t\||)$ for all units $a,t$. Third, for all units $a,t$ with $t\neq1$ and $t\in U$, for every Haar measure $\tau$ on the centralizer of $\gamma=\mathrm{diag}(a,at)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ (Borel structure) giving mass $1$ to the elements of that centralizer whose matrix and inverse matrix have entries in $\mathcal{O}_v$, and for every $J\in\mathbb{C}$ that is a weighted orbital integral of $f$ at $\gamma$ against $\tau$ (an integral of $f(x^{-1}\gamma x)$ times the local weight and a section function against the local Haar measure), both of the following hold: (a) for all units $\alpha,\beta$ of $L\otimes_K K_v$ such that the $\sigma$-norm string $\prod_{i<[L:K]}\sigma^i(\mathrm{diag}(\alpha,\beta))$ equals the image of $\gamma$ under the base-change map $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)\to\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$, for every Haar measure $\tau'$ on the $\sigma$-twisted centralizer $\{x: x\delta\sigma(x)^{-1}=\delta\}$ of $\delta=\mathrm{diag}(\alpha,\beta)$ giving mass $1$ to the semi-local integral set, and every $J'$ that is a twisted weighted orbital integral of $\varphi$ at $\delta$ against $\tau'$, one has $\|1-t\|\cdot\sqrt{\|a\|/\|at\|}\,\bigl(J'-[L:K]\,J\bigr)=\Psi(a,t)$; and (b) if no such $\alpha,\beta$ exist, then $\|1-t\|\cdot\sqrt{\|a\|/\|at\|}\,\bigl(0-[L:K]\,J\bigr)=\Psi(a,t)$.
--
--   This is the local input, at a finite place $v$, for the comparison of the twisted trace formula for the cyclic extension $L/K$ of prime degree with the trace formula for $K$: the normalised difference between the twisted weighted orbital integral of $\varphi$ and $[L:K]$ times the weighted orbital integral of $f$ at a split regular class $\mathrm{diag}(a,at)$ is realised by a single function $\Psi$ of $(a,t)$ which is constant on multiplicative cells around $(a,t)$ and has a logarithmic germ bound at $t=1$. It is used by the statements that produce compactly supported versions of this discrepancy function and by the summation of local class contributions over windows.
